<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49828" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰδῐ-άζω</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἴδιος</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be alone</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdn.
				4.12.7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				7.6.7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				66.9
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰδιάζουσαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Herod.
					6
				</span></i>
			 tit.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δωμάτιον ἰδιάζον</span>
			<i>secluded</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hld.
				7.12
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰ. πρός τινα</span>
			<i>to be alone</i> with . . , ib.<i><span class="en">
				25
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰ. θεῷ</span>
			<i>to be alone with</i> God, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.95
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰ. πράγματι</span>
			<i>devote oneself</i> to a thing, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Com.Adesp.</u>
				414
			</span></i>:—so in 
				Med.
			, of members of a chorus, <i>sing independently</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				922a35
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>to be peculiar</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰδιάζοντα γένη λίθων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Sign.</u>
					28
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Jul.
				<u>Gal.</u>
				143a
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰ. τῇ φύσει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					2.58
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰδιάζουσα φύσις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					3.46
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hld.
				2.28
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰδιάζον συμπόσιον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ath.
					1.12a
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ ἰδιάζουσαι ἀρχαί</span>
			<i>special</i> principles, <i><span class="en">
				Dam.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				134
			</span></i>; of drugs, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰδιάζων</span>
			<i>special, superior</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				1.14
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἃ ἂν ἰδιάσωμεν, ψευδόμεθα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.E.
					<u>M.</u>
					7.133
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰ. τινί</span>
			<i>to be peculiarly adapted</i> to . . , <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>NA</u>
				6.19
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βωμὸς τῷ Διονύσῳ ἰδιάζων</span>
			<i>appropriated</i> to <i><span class="en">
				D.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hld.
				10.6
			</span></i>: c. gen., <i>to be the property of</i>, <i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>AJ</u>
				16.7.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ -άζουσα θερμασία</span> its
			<i>proper</i> heat, <i><span class="en">
				Herod.Med.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				5.30.12
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> Gramm.,
				<i>to be peculiar to an individual</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ κτητικὰ -άζει κατὰ τὸν κτήτορα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.D.
					<u>Pron.</u>
					105.4
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Synt.</u>
				128.13
			</span></i>, al.:—so in 
				Med.
			, [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ βασιλεὺς] μᾶλλον -άζεται
				τοῦ Πτολεμαίου</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				84.20
			</span></i>.</div>
